WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.166
Have you

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.626
seen this insane video

00:00:01.626 --> 00:00:03.211
of a giant Chinese Coast

00:00:03.211 --> 00:00:03.712
Guard boat

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:06.131
ramming into a smaller boat

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:06.965
from the Philippines?

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:08.174
This is just one part of China's

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.467
strategy to control

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:10.552
the South China Sea,

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:12.178
which is this really valuable water,

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:14.180
which China claims almost all of.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:14.514
Now, of course,

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.348
no one in the world

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.808
recognizes this claim.

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:17.517
And all of China's

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.602
neighbors have claims that cut through

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:20.311
China's claim.

00:00:20.311 --> 00:00:21.354
That Filipino boat

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:22.689
that was run into by the Chinese

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.691
Coast Guard was actually in Filipino

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:25.859
economic waters.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:26.693
But crucially,

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.361
this boat was carrying supplies

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:30.030
to a tiny little island

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:30.655
where the Philippines

00:00:30.655 --> 00:00:32.073
has intentionally crashed

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:33.742
an old warship to kind of plant

00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:35.493
a flag and claim it as theirs.

00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:36.327
And there's a bunch of sailors

00:00:36.327 --> 00:00:37.579
who just live out here.

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:38.705
China does not like this.

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.999
Hence, going and bullying the supply ship

00:00:40.999 --> 00:00:42.333
that's going to refuel them.

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:43.835
China has their own island

00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:45.211
building operation,

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.921
which they use to put military assets

00:00:46.921 --> 00:00:48.089
all over the South China Sea.

00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:48.798
And every year

00:00:48.798 --> 00:00:49.466
they get more

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:50.550
and more aggressive

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.010
in asserting their dominance

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.261
over the entire South

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:53.887
China Sea,

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.847
which could very easily escalate

00:00:55.847 --> 00:00:57.140
into a broader conflict.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:57.891
If you want to better understand

00:00:57.891 --> 00:00:59.726
global politics, follow along for more.

